I agree we should just unexpose the method on master. The method binding seems to be used only because of an internal call (see https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/46003#issuecomment-810003807).

@rafallus If you're up for refactoring this fix, the proper changes are:
* Modify `body_set_force_integration_callback` in the physics server to use a callable:
https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/35066f39ff111ee0e9d4aba534bb08fc2d686156/servers/physics_server_3d.h#L489
```
virtual void body_set_force_integration_callback(RID p_body, const Callable &p_callable, const Variant &p_udata = Variant()) = 0; 
```
* Modify how it's stored in the body inside the physics server:
https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/35066f39ff111ee0e9d4aba534bb08fc2d686156/servers/physics_3d/body_3d_sw.h#L129-L133
```
struct ForceIntegrationCallback {
	Callable callable;
	Variant udata;
};
```
* Modify the call to use `Callable::get_object()` and `Callable::call()`:
https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/35066f39ff111ee0e9d4aba534bb08fc2d686156/servers/physics_3d/body_3d_sw.cpp#L696-L705
* Make the same changes in Bullet module and Godot Physics 2D
* Use `callable_mp` macro in calls to `body_set_force_integration_callback`
* Remove all the `_direct_state_changed` bindings
